## Evidence gaps the brief did not close

- Whether MWAA is currently IPAWS-authorized at IAD and DCA, and which
  agency holds the origination authority.
- Current STI performance data (if any) from MWAA's existing voice-
  evacuation systems at IAD Concourses A/B/C/D and DCA Terminals 1/2.
- Whether MWAA has ever executed an occupied-condition STI acceptance
  test on a completed terminal project.
- Whether the 2025 Use & Lease MII language treats "passenger-experience"
  or "design manual" changes as airline-review triggers, and therefore
  whether a quiet-by-design standard requires MII concurrence.
- Employee sound-exposure monitoring practice for MWAA and tenant staff
  in the noisiest concourse zones at both airports.

These are surfaced as open questions rather than answered by inference. A
public safety brief that guesses at any of them is the brief that gets
quoted in the wrong deposition.
